{
  "$comment": [
    "Acceptance dataset for the Fit Finder size engine (audit 2026-09-21:",
    "'أضف بيانات قبول مجهولة لعدة أجسام ومقاسات وبراندات، مع expected range لا مقاس واحد فقط').",
    "",
    "Every case is ANONYMOUS synthetic anthropometry - no real user data, nothing",
    "from the production database. Each case states an ACCEPTABLE SET of sizes,",
    "not one size: real sizing has legitimate adjacent-size answers, and a test",
    "that demands a single label would encode overconfidence into the suite.",
    "",
    "Charts here are deliberately different per brand so the suite proves the",
    "engine uses the product's own chart: 'atlas' runs generous, 'borea' runs",
    "small, 'ceder' publishes finished-garment measurements, 'delta' publishes",
    "nothing (standards fallback), 'echo' publishes in inches.",
    "",
    "expected_confidence_max/min are bounds, not equalities - they pin the",
    "DIRECTION of the honesty properties (estimates must not look measured)",
    "without freezing arbitrary constants."
  ],
